                <pb facs="0858" n="851" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg851"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.94244/189: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-01-23T17:00:00+09:00">January 23, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 23—7:18 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>20. Department’s 12, January 22, 7 p.m., smuggling in China. I consider the
                    moment not opportune for an approach to the Japanese Government. Clive concurs.
                    I shall watch situation and advise later.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
